Thanks to "Steven" who Hearsed a bones file for
Knight Quest "L" bones file, my long drought in
acquiring new unique types of bones files ends and
Hearse adds another type to my collection.

Since I've been contributing like crazy (yes, I
really am that bad a player[*]), my count of extant
contributed files on the Hearse server has crept up
to 87 from 72 at my last report, with a bit of
normal lossage along the way as older bones files
get dropped by the server.

I now have 107 unique types of bones files, with
still several holes.

Go thou and Hearse, folks!

It's just _lots_ more fun to find a stranger's bones
file then your own.

Meanwhile, I'd built up so much credit for files
contributed for which none could be repaid because
no new type instances existed in Hearse, that I
started removing some high level dungeon bones file
types for which I had only a single instance, from
Hearse's sight, to gather a second instance to keep
alongside the first, just to burn up those credits.

I have multiple instances of lots of bones file
types, especially the early levels, of course, so
my total collection right now is 261 bones files.

Life is good, sort of in a funny way.

